 "case": {
  "annotations": {
   "notes": [
    "Both forks ring reliably BEFORE either is PRACKed, so the PRACKs interleave: each must ride its own early dialog, carry that fork's To-tag, and number from the INVITE's CSeq in that fork's own space (RFC 3261 \u00a712.2.1.1, RFC 3262 \u00a77.2).",
    "The caller's expects observe the forks as r1/r2 \u2014 the a-facing tags the system mints \u2014 while the callee answers under the minted f1/f2.",
    "The 486 answers under f1's tag, so the attempt ends where a forking callee's losing forks end: no dialog confirms."
   ]
  },
  "family": "transparent",
  "id": "forked-ring-interleaved",
